-moduledoc """
SHAKE128 (FIPS 202) is an extendable-output function (XOF) built on
the Keccak-f[1600] permutation with 24 rounds. It hashes an input of
any length into an output of any requested length and offers 128-bit
security against collision and preimage attacks.

The standard domain byte `domain_standard/0` (`16#1F`) produces
SHAKE128 as specified; `init_with_domain/1` accepts another domain
byte to derive an independent, non-standard function for domain
separation.

The streaming functions thread an opaque `t:state/0` through `init/0`,
`update/2`, and `squeeze/2`. Every call returns a new state and leaves its
argument unchanged. Squeezing continues the output stream: consecutive
`squeeze/2` calls on the returned states produce the same bytes as one
longer squeeze, so output can be read incrementally. Updates over large
inputs yield to other processes between chunks.

```erlang
Out = libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128:crypto_xof_shake128(32, <<"hello world">>),
32 = byte_size(Out),
State0 = libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128:init(),
State1 = libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128:update(State0, <<"hello ">>),
State2 = libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128:update(State1, <<"world">>),
{State3, First} = libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128:squeeze(State2, 16),
{_State4, Second} = libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128:squeeze(State3, 16),
Out = <<First/binary, Second/binary>>.
```
""".
